  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 155 AM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe latter half of the work week will start off on a cloudy note \nWednesday night through Thursday, due to the continued cyclonic flow \nover the region. Some guidance suggests we could even see some \nsunshine Thursday, but with the upper-level system/cyclonic flow \nstill in place, I've leaned towards a mostly cloudy forecast. Some \noccasional showers also remain possible. Things look to finally dry \nout by Friday as an area of high pressure and upper-level ridging \ndevelops. We appear more likely to see some peeks of sunshine by \nthen.\n\nAs we look ahead towards the upcoming weekend into early next week, \nthere's not much of note, thanks to an amplified upper-level ridge \nthat's progged to develop over the Intermountain West states. This \nwill help block any shortwaves from translating over our region, \nresulting in a dry forecast. Average to slightly above average \ntemperatures will be common during this time frame, with highs in \nthe middle to upper 50s and lows in the upper 30s.",
